                <pb facs="0318" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6775/541.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Enrique C.
                            Creel to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chihuahua, Mexico</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I very highly appreciate the honor of your congratulations upon my return from
                    Central America. Your excellent work is well understood, and your name is
                    cherished by the people who are already enjoying the great benefits of peace,
                    order, and civilization.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Enrique C. Creel.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
